; top_amount() of a balance is its first component in commodity order,
; whatever order the commodities were posted in.
;
; The manual defines top_amount by commodity sort order.  $ sorts before
; CAD and EUR, so once $10.00 is in the running total it stays on top,
; although EUR was posted first and CAD last.  top_amount() used to take
; whichever component the balance happened to keep first, 3 CAD or 5 EUR
; on the last line; the order in which a balance keeps its components
; changes from run to run, so top_amount() now picks by commodity order.
; With three commodities neither posting order (5 EUR) nor its reverse
; (3 CAD) can pass for commodity order on the last line.

2024/01/01 Payee
    Expenses:Food    5 EUR
    Expenses:Food    $10.00
    Expenses:Food    3 CAD
    Assets:Cash

test reg --format '%(top_amount(total))\n' Expenses
5 EUR
$10.00
$10.00
end test
